# Act 3: Depot CI — content plan

Status: planned. Acts 1–2 run; act 3 is unwired. Captured 2026-08-26.

## The idea

This rig becomes a free deep-dive for Joel's channel: "we built our own GitHub."
Not an ad. The piece explains Depot in depth by using it, not by reading its
homepage. It also serves as a reference for what a deep product explanation
looks like, for anyone briefing creators on CI/CD products.

## Narrative arc

- **Cold open** — the 2026-08-17 GitHub outage: ~7.5 hours, PRs, Actions, and
  webhooks down. Pushes worked; nobody could review, merge, or deploy.
  (Also 2026-08-06: Actions degraded fleet-wide.) `needs_source` links in the
  script draft before recording.
- **Act 1 (runs)** — the forge is a binary and a bucket. walgit + MinIO on a
  NAS, converged by the `NasMinio` alchemy provider.
- **Act 2 (runs)** — the bucket is fungible. Same walgit config pointed at
  Cloudflare R2. Zero egress, conditional writes, nothing else changes.
- **Act 3 (planned)** — the part we refuse to build: CI. walgit's per-repo
  webhooks fire Depot CI. Forge you own, bucket you rent, CI you don't build.

## Why Depot fits the story

- Depot CI is its own engine with its own control plane — the decoupling
  answer to "okay, but Actions?" that acts 1–2 set up.
- `depot build` works with no forge in the loop at all: the escape-hatch demo
  (CI host down, build locally, ship anyway).
- Per-second billing ($0.0001/s, no one-minute minimum) is a demo-able claim.
- Fresh surface, 2026: Depot CI GA'd in March; remote agent sandboxes and a
  Sandbox SDK exist. The agent angle stacks on top if wanted.

## Honesty rails

- Depot-hosted GitHub Actions runners do NOT survive a GitHub Actions outage —
  they take jobs from GitHub's control plane. Only Depot CI, local
  `depot build`, and sandboxes are decoupled. Never blur this on camera.
- The claim is decoupling, not invincibility: Depot published its own
  us-east-1 postmortem. "Never goes down" is a liability, not a pitch.
- Reproduce any speed number in this rig before repeating it. A measured 11x
  beats a quoted "up to 40x."

## Gating spike (do first)

Wire walgit webhook → Depot CI and get one push-to-build-receipt round trip.
Unverified (`needs_source`): whether Depot CI accepts arbitrary external
webhook/API triggers cleanly, and what the auth handshake looks like.
Until this round-trips, the piece has two acts and a promise.

## Recording boundary

Operator topology stays out of frame the same way it stays out of this repo
(see VISION.md boundaries). Lead on-camera with the R2 act, or record the NAS
act with paths and hosts generalized. Decide before recording, not in the edit.

## Format

One long-form deep dive. Build-in-public posts fall out of wiring act 3 and
test the framing before the video does. Audience comments on the free piece
are angle research: what gets pushed back on, what gets clipped, where people
ask "what's Depot?"
